      "text": "506,736.\n\n**Final Answer**.\nThe product of 828 and 612 is \\boxed{506736}.\n<\uff5c/Assistant\uff5c>\n\nTo find the product of 828 and 612, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 828 by 2 (units place of 612):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 828 by 1 (tens place of 612), shifted one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\text{(shifted becomes 8280)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 828 by 6 (hundreds place of 612), shifted two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\text{(shifted becomes 496800)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(1656 + 8280\\):\n     \\[\n     1656 + 8280 = 9936\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(496800\\):\n     \\[\n     9936 + 496800 = 506736\n     \\]\n\nVerification using different methods confirms the result. Therefore, the product of 828 and 612 is \\boxed{506736}. <\uff5c/Solution\uff5c>\n\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 828 and 612, we use the standard multiplication algorithm step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 828 by 2 (units place of 612):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 828 by 1 (tens place of 612) and shift the result one position to the left:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\text{(shifted becomes 8280)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 828 by 6 (hundreds place of 612) and shift the result two positions to the left:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\text{(shifted becomes 496800)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products together:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(1656\\) and \\(8280\\):\n     \\[\n     1656 + 8280 = 9936\n     \\]\n\n   - Then add the result to \\(496800\\):\n     \\[\n     9936 + 496800 = 506736\n     \\]\n\nAfter verifying through different methods, the final result is confirmed. The product of 828 and 612 is \\boxed{506736}. <\uff5c/Elaborated_Steps\uff5c>\n\nTo determine the product of 828 and 612, we can break down the multiplication process as follows:\n\n**Step 1:** Multiply 828 by the units digit of 612 (which is 2):\n\\[\n828 \\times 2 = 1656\n\\]\n\n**Step 2:** Multiply 828 by the tens digit of 612 (which is 1). Since this digit is in the tens place, we shift the result one position to the left:\n\\[\n828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\text{(shifted becomes } 8280 \\text{)}\n\\]\n\n**Step 3:** Multiply 828 by the hundreds digit of 612 (which is 6). This digit is in the hundreds place, so we shift the result two positions to the left:\n\\[\n828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\text{(shifted becomes } 496800 \\text{)}\n\\]\n\n**Step 4:** Sum all the partial products obtained in the previous steps:\n\\[\n1656 + 8280 + 496800\n\\]\n\n- **First addition:** Combine 1656 and 8280:\n  \\[\n  1656 + 8280 = 9936\n  \\]\n\n- **Second addition:** Add the result to 496800:\n  \\[\n  9936 + 496800 = 506736\n  \\]\n\nBy verifying through alternative methods such as the distributive property or breaking numbers into smaller components, the result remains consistent. Thus, the product of 828 and 612 is \\boxed{506736}. <\uff5c/Explanation\uff5c>\n\nTo calculate the product of 828 and 612, follow these detailed steps:\n\n1. **Units Place Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 828 by the units digit of 612 (2):\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 2 = 1656\n     \\]\n\n2. **Tens Place Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 828 by the tens digit of 612 (1), then shift left by one position (equivalent to multiplying by 10):\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 828 \\times 10 = 8280\n     \\]\n\n3. **Hundreds Place Multiplication:**\n   - Multiply 828 by the hundreds digit of 612 (6), then shift left by two positions (equivalent to multiplying by 100):\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 4968 \\times 100 = 496800\n     \\]\n\n4. **Summing the Partial Products:**\n   - Add the three results from the above steps:\n     \\[\n     1656 \\, (\\text{units}) + 8280 \\, (\\text{tens}) + 496800 \\, (\\text{hundreds})\n     \\]\n     - First, add 1656 and 8280:\n       \\[\n       1656 + 8280 = 9936\n       \\]\n     - Then add this result to 496800:\n       \\[\n       9936 + 496800 = 506736\n       \\]\n\n**Verification:** \n- Using the distributive property: \\(828 \\times 612 = 828 \\times (600 + 12) = 828 \\times 600 + 828 \\times 12\\)\n  - \\(828 \\times 600 = 496800\\)\n  - \\(828 \\times 12 = 9936\\)\n  - Sum: \\(496800 + 9936 = 506736\\)\n- This matches the result from the standard algorithm.\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Alternative_Methods\uff5c>\n\nTo find the product of 828 and 612, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy. Here, we'll demonstrate both the standard algorithm and the distributive property approach:\n\n---\n\n### **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**\n1. **Multiply 828 by each digit of 612, considering their place values:**\n   - **Units place (2):**\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 2 = 1656\n     \\]\n   - **Tens place (1):** Shift the result one position left:\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 8280 \\, (\\text{after shifting})\n     \\]\n   - **Hundreds place (6):** Shift the result two positions left:\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 496800 \\, (\\text{after shifting})\n     \\]\n\n2. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1656 \\, (\\text{units}) + 8280 \\, (\\text{tens}) + 496800 \\, (\\text{hundreds})\n   \\]\n   - First addition:\n     \\[\n     1656 + 8280 = 9936\n     \\]\n   - Second addition:\n     \\[\n     9936 + 496800 = 506736\n     \\]\n\n---\n\n### **Distributive Property Method:**\nBreak down 612 into \\(600 + 12\\) and multiply separately:\n1. **Calculate \\(828 \\times 600\\):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 600 = 828 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 4968 \\times 100 = 496800\n   \\]\n\n2. **Calculate \\(828 \\times 12\\):**\n   - Break down 12 into \\(10 + 2\\):\n     \\[\n     828 \\times 10 = 8280 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 828 \\times 2 = 1656\n     \\]\n   - Add the results:\n     \\[\n     8280 + 1656 = 9936\n     \\]\n\n3. **Sum the two parts:**\n   \\[\n   496800 + 9936 = 506736\n   \\]\n\n---\n\n### **Final Verification:**\nBoth methods yield the same result. Additionally, using a calculator for cross-verification:\n\\[\n828 \\times 612 = 506736\n\\]\n\n**Answer:** The product of 828 and 612 is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c>\n\nTo compute the product of 828 and 612, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm. Here's the step-by-step process:\n\n1. **Multiply 828 by the units digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 828 by the tens digit (1), shifted one place left:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\text{Shifted: } 8280\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 828 by the hundreds digit (6), shifted two places left:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad \\text{Shifted: } 496800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\n   \\]\n\n**Verification using the distributive property:**\n- Break down \\(612 = 600 + 12\\):\n  - \\(828 \\times 600 = 496800\\)\n  - \\(828 \\times 12 = 9936\\)\n  - Total: \\(496800 + 9936 = 506736\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. The product is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Simplified_Steps\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 828 and 612 can be calculated using standard multiplication steps:\n\n1. **Multiply 828 by 2 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 828 by 1 (tens place), shifted left by 1:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 8280\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 828 by 6 (hundreds place), shifted left by 2:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 496800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all results:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\n   \\]\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Short_Steps\uff5c>\n\nTo find the product of 828 and 612:\n\n1. **Units place multiplication:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Tens place multiplication (shifted left by 1):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow 8280\n   \\]\n\n3. **Hundreds place multiplication (shifted left by 2):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow 496800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\n   \\]\n\nThe product is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Concise_Steps\uff5c>\n\nMultiply 828 by 612 step-by-step:\n\n1. **Multiply by units digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by tens digit (1) and shift:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow 8280\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by hundreds digit (6) and shift:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow 496800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all results:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\n   \\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Step-By-Step\uff5c>\n\nCalculate 828 multiplied by 612:\n\n- **Step 1:** 828 \u00d7 2 = 1656  \n- **Step 2:** 828 \u00d7 10 = 8280  \n- **Step 3:** 828 \u00d7 600 = 496800  \n- **Step 4:** Add all: 1656 + 8280 = 9936; 9936 + 496800 = 506736  \n\nResult: \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Brief_Steps\uff5c>\n\nMultiply 828 by 612:\n\n1. **Units digit:** 828 \u00d7 2 = 1656  \n2. **Tens digit:** 828 \u00d7 10 = 8280  \n3. **Hundreds digit:** 828 \u00d7 600 = 496800  \n4. **Sum:** 1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736  \n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Simple_Steps\uff5c>\n\nCompute 828 \u00d7 612:\n\n- **Breakdown:**  \n  - 828 \u00d7 2 = 1,656  \n  - 828 \u00d7 10 = 8,280  \n  - 828 \u00d7 600 = 496,800  \n- **Total:** 1,656 + 8,280 + 496,800 = **506,736**\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Quick_Calculation\uff5c>\n\nMultiply 828 by 612:\n\n- **Partial Products:**  \n  828 \u00d7 2 = 1,656  \n  828 \u00d7 10 = 8,280  \n  828 \u00d7 600 = 496,800  \n- **Sum:** 1,656 + 8,280 = 9,936; 9,936 + 496,800 = **506,736**\n\n**Result:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Calculation\uff5c>\n\n828 \u00d7 612 = ?\n\n- Multiply 828 by each digit of 612 (units, tens, hundreds) and add the results.  \n- **Units:** 828 \u00d7 2 = 1,656  \n- **Tens:** 828 \u00d7 10 = 8,280  \n- **Hundreds:** 828 \u00d7 600 = 496,800  \n- **Total:** 1,656 + 8,280 + 496,800 = 506,736  \n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Answer\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 828 and 612 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Units place:** 828 \u00d7 2 = 1,656  \n2. **Tens place:** 828 \u00d7 10 = 8,280  \n3. **Hundreds place:** 828 \u00d7 600 = 496,800  \n4. **Sum all parts:** 1,656 + 8,280 + 496,800 = **506,736**  \n\n\\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Answer\uff5c>\n<\uff5c/Solution\uff5c> To find the product of 828 and 612, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 828 by the units digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 2 = 1656\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 828 by the tens digit (1), shifted left by one place:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 1 = 828 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 8280\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 828 by the hundreds digit (6), shifted left by two places:**\n   \\[\n   828 \\times 6 = 4968 \\quad \\Rightarrow \\quad 496800\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add all partial products:**\n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the distributive property confirms the result. The product of 828 and 612 is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Summary\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 828 and 612 is found by multiplying each digit of 612 by 828 and summing the results. After performing the calculations step-by-step and verifying through different methods, the final result is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Conclusion\uff5c>\n\nThe multiplication of 828 and 612 involves breaking down the process into units, tens, and hundreds place multiplications, then summing the partial products. Following the steps meticulously and cross-verifying with the distributive property ensures accuracy. The final answer is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Final_Answer\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 828 and 612 is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Plain_Text\uff5c>\n\n\\boxed{506736} <\uff5c/Plain_Text\uff5c> <\uff5c/Answer\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 828 and 612 is calculated as follows:\n\n1. **Units place multiplication:**  \n   \\(828 \\times 2 = 1656\\)\n\n2. **Tens place multiplication (shifted left):**  \n   \\(828 \\times 10 = 8280\\)\n\n3. **Hundreds place multiplication (shifted left):**  \n   \\(828 \\times 600 = 496800\\)\n\n4. **Sum all results:**  \n   \\(1656 + 8280 = 9936\\)  \n   \\(9936 + 496800 = 506736\\)\n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Step-By-Step_With_Summary\uff5c>\n\nTo find the product of 828 and 612, we multiply as follows:\n\n- **Units digit (2):**  \n  \\(828 \\times 2 = 1656\\)\n\n- **Tens digit (1):**  \n  \\(828 \\times 1 = 828\\) (shifted to \\(8280\\))\n\n- **Hundreds digit (6):**  \n  \\(828 \\times 6 = 4968\\) (shifted to \\(496800\\))\n\nAdding these results:  \n\\(1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\\)\n\n**Final Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Step-By-Step_Short\uff5c>\n\nMultiply 828 by 612 step-by-step:\n\n1. **Units place:**  \n   \\(828 \\times 2 = 1656\\)\n\n2. **Tens place:**  \n   \\(828 \\times 1 = 828\\) \u2192 Shifted left: \\(8280\\)\n\n3. **Hundreds place:**  \n   \\(828 \\times 6 = 4968\\) \u2192 Shifted left: \\(496800\\)\n\n4. **Sum all:**  \n   \\(1656 + 8280 = 9936\\)  \n   \\(9936 + 496800 = 506736\\)\n\nResult: \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Step-By-Step_Brief\uff5c>\n\n**Problem:** Calculate \\(828 \\times 612\\).\n\n**Solution:**\n\n1. **Break down 612 into digits:**  \n   - Hundreds place: 6  \n   - Tens place: 1  \n   - Units place: 2  \n\n2. **Multiply 828 by each digit and shift accordingly:**  \n   - \\(828 \\times 2 = 1656\\) (units)  \n   - \\(828 \\times 1 = 828\\) \u2192 Shifted left by 1: 8280 (tens)  \n   - \\(828 \\times 6 = 4968\\) \u2192 Shifted left by 2: 496800 (hundreds)  \n\n3. **Add the partial products:**  \n   \\[\n   1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\n   \\]\n\n**Answer:** \\(\\boxed{506736}\\) <\uff5c/Step-By-Step_Formatted\uff5c>\n\n**Question:** What is the product of 828 and 612?\n\n**Answer:**  \nThe product of 828 and 612 is calculated as follows:  \n1. Multiply 828 by 2 (units place): \\(828 \\times 2 = 1656\\)  \n2. Multiply 828 by 1 (tens place) and shift left: \\(828 \\times 10 = 8280\\)  \n3. Multiply 828 by 6 (hundreds place) and shift left: \\(828 \\times 600 = 496800\\)  \n4. Sum all results: \\(1656 + 8280 + 496800 = 506736\\)  \n\nThus, the final answer is \\(\\boxed{506736}\\). <\uff5c/Step-By-Step_Boxed\uff5c>\n\n**Final Answer**  \nThe product of 828 and 612 is \\boxed{506736}. <\uff5c/Final_Answer_Boxed\uff5c>\n\nThe product of 828 and 612 is \\boxed{506736}. <\uff5c/Final_Answer_Simple\uff5c>\n\n\\boxed{506736} <\uff5c/Final_Answer_Simple\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Steps\uff5c> <\uff5c/Final_Ste