final_output:  ['85,086.\n\n<｜Assistant｜>.\n\n\nTo find the product of 174 and 489, we can use the distributive property and break down the multiplication into smaller parts:\n\n1. **Breakdown using the distributive property:**\n   - **174 × 400** = 69,600  \n     *(174 × 4 = 696; 696 × 100 = 69,600)*\n   - **174 × 80** = 13,920  \n     *(174 × 8 = 1,392; 1,392 × 10 = 13,920)*\n   - **174 × 9** = 1,566  \n     *(170 × 9 = 1,530 + 4 × 9 = 36; 1,530 + 36 = 1,566)*\n\n2. **Sum the results:**\n   ```\n   69,600  \n   +13,920  \n   +1,566  \n   = 85,086\n   ```\n\n3. **Verification via standard multiplication:**\n   ```\n       174  \n     ×489  \n     -----  \n      1,566  (174 × 9)  \n     13,920  (174 × 80)  \n    +69,600  (174 × 400)  \n    ---------  \n     85,086  \n   ```\n\n4. **Alternative method (prime factors):**\n   - **174 = 2 × 3 × 29**  \n   - **489 = 3 × 163**  \n   - Multiply all factors:  \n     *(2 × 3 × 29) × (3 × 163) = 2 × 3² × 29 × 163 = 85,086*\n\n**Final Answer:**  \nThe product of 174 and 489 is \\boxed{85086}.', '']
