final_output:  ["347,480. ｜\n\nWait, let me double-check that. Maybe I made an error in addition?\n\nHmm, let me add them again step by step. First, 4,760 plus 57,120. 4,760 plus 50,000 is 54,760, then plus 7,120 gives 61,880. Then adding 285,600 to that: 61,880 plus 200,000 is 261,880, plus 85,600 equals 347,480. Okay, that checks out. So the final answer is 347,480.\n\nBut just to be thorough, maybe use another method? Let's try breaking down the numbers:\n\n365 is 300 + 60 + 5. So 952*(300+60+5) = 952*300 + 952*60 + 952*5.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n- 952 * 300: 952 * 3 = 2,856, so times 100 is 285,600.\n\n- 952 * 60: 952 * 6 = 5,712, times 10 is 57,120.\n\n- 952 *5 = 4,760. Adding all together: same as before, 285,600 + 57,120 = 342,720; then +4,760 = 347,480. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property another way? Let's see:\n\n952 * 365. Let me think of 952 as 900 + 52.\n\nSo, (900 + 52)*365 = 900*365 + 52*365.\n\nCalculate 900*365:\n\nFirst, 9*365 = 3,285. Then times 100 is 328,500.\n\nThen 52*365: Let's compute that. 50*365 = 18,250; 2*365=730. So total is 18,250 +730=18,980.\n\nAdding to the previous: 328,500 +18,980 = 347,480. Same answer again. Okay, definitely confident now.\n\nAlternatively, use calculator verification? Since I can't use a calculator, but let me do another method. Maybe 952*365 = ?\n\nLet me reverse the multiplication: 365*952.\n\nMultiply 365 by 900: 365*9=3,285, so times 100 is 328,500.\n\n365*50: 365*5=1,825, times 10 is 18,250.\n\n365*2=730. Adding those together: 328,500+18,250=346,750 +730=347,480. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 347,480. I think that's solid. All methods cross-check to the same answer. So I can be sure that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 952 and 365 is \\boxed{347480}.\n｜\n\nTo find the product of 952 and 365, we use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using multiple methods:\n\n1. **Multiply 952 by 5 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 5 = 4760\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 952 by 6 (tens place) and shift one position left:**\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 6 = 5712 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one: 57120)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 952 by 3 (hundreds place) and shift two positions left:**\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 3 = 2856 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two: 285600)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     4760 \\\\\n    +57120 \\\\\n    +285600 \\\\\n    \\hline\n     347480 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - Adding 4760 and 57120:\n     \\[\n     4760 + 57120 = 61880\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to 285600:\n     \\[\n     61880 + 285600 = 347480\n     \\]\n\n5. **Verification using different methods:**\n   - Breaking down 365 into 300 + 60 + 5:\n     \\[\n     952 \\times 300 = 285600, \\quad 952 \\times 60 = 57120, \\quad 952 \\times 5 = 4760\n     \\]\n     Summing these:\n     \\[\n     285600 + 57120 + 4760 = 347480\n     \\]\n\n   - Breaking down 952 into 900 + 52:\n     \\[\n     900 \\times 365 = 328500, \\quad 52 \\times 365 = 18980\n     \\]\n     Summing these:\n     \\[\n     328500 + 18980 = 347480\n     \\]\n\n   - Reversing the multiplication (365 × 952):\n     \\[\n     365 \\times 900 = 328500, \\quad 365 \\times 50 = 18250, \\quad 365 \\times 2 = 730\n     \\]\n     Summing these:\n     \\[\n     328500 + 18250 + 730 = 347480\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\nThe product of 952 and 365 is \\boxed{347480}.｜\n\n\nTo find the product of 952 and 365, we use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using multiple methods:\n\n1. **Multiply 952 by 5 (units place):**\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 5 = 4760\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 952 by 6 (tens place) and shift one position left:**\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 6 = 5712 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by one: 57120)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 952 by 3 (hundreds place) and shift two positions left:**\n   \\[\n   952 \\times 3 = 2856 \\quad \\text{(shifted left by two: 285600)}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Add the results of the three multiplications:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{array}{r}\n     4760 \\\\\n    +57120 \\\\\n    +285600 \\\\\n    \\hline\n     347480 \\\\\n   \\end{array}\n   \\]\n   - Adding 4760 and 57120:\n     \\[\n     4760 + 57120 = 61880\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to 285600:\n     \\[\n     61880 + 285600 = 347480\n     \\]\n\n5. **Verification using different methods:**\n   - Breaking down 365 into 300 + 60 + 5:\n     \\[\n     952 \\times 300 = 285600, \\quad 952 \\times 60 = 57120, \\quad 952 \\times 5 = 4760\n     \\]\n     Summing these:\n     \\[\n     285600 + 57120 + 4760 = 347480\n     \\]\n\n   - Breaking down 952 into 900 + 52:\n     \\[\n     900 \\times 365 = 328500, \\quad 52 \\times 365 = 18980\n     \\]\n     Summing these:\n     \\[\n     328500 + 18980 = 347480\n     \\]\n\n   - Reversing the multiplication (365 × 952):\n     \\[\n     365 \\times 900 = 328500, \\quad 365 \\times 50 = 18250, \\quad 365 \\times 2 = 730\n     \\]\n     Summing these:\n     \\[\n     328500 + 18250 + 730 = 347480\n     \\]\n\nAll methods confirm the result is consistent. \n\nThe product of 952 and 365 is \\boxed{347480}.", '']  5%|5         | 25/500 [2:49:59<54:15:54, 411.27s/it]
