tiply 391 \u00d7 50**:\n   - Compute 391 \u00d7 5:\n     - 300 \u00d7 5 = 1,500\n     - 90 \u00d7 5 = 450\n     - 1 \u00d7 5 = 5\n     - Total: 1,500 + 450 + 5 = 1,955\n   - Add a zero for the tens place: **19,550** (second partial product).\n\nNow, the hundreds place (2), representing 200:\n\n3. **Multiply 391 \u00d7 200**:\n   - Compute 391 \u00d7 2:\n     - 300 \u00d7 2 = 600\n     - 90 \u00d7 2 = 180\n     - 1 \u00d7 2 = 2\n     - Total: 600 + 180 + 2 = 782\n   - Add two zeros: **78,200** (third partial product).\n\n**Adding all partial products**:\n- First two: 391 + 19,550 = **19,941**\n- Add the third: 19,941 + 78,200 = **98,141**\n\n**Verification via distributive property**:\nBreak down:\n- **391 = 400 - 9**\n- **251 = 250 + 1**\n\nExpand:\n\\[\n(400 - 9)(250 + 1) = 400\u00d7250 + 400\u00d71 - 9\u00d7250 - 9\u00d71\n\\]\n\nCalculations:\n1. **400 \u00d7 250 = 100,000**\n2. **400 \u00d7 1 = 400**\n3. **-9 \u00d7 250 = -2,250**\n4. **-9 \u00d7 1 = -9**\n\nSumming:\n- 100,000 + 400 = 100,400\n- 100,400 - 2,250 = 98,150\n- 98,150 - 9 = **98,141**\n\n**Division Check**:\nDivide 98,141 by 391:\n- **391 \u00d7 200 = 78,200** \u2192 Subtract: 98,141 - 78,200 = 19,941\n- **391 \u00d7 50 = 19,550** \u2192 Subtract: 19,941 - 19,550 = 391\n- **391 \u00d7 1 = 391** \u2192 Subtract: 0\n- Total multiplier: **251**\n\nAll methods confirm the result.\n\n**Final Answer:** \\boxed{98141}\n<\uff5c/History\uff5c> <\uff5c/User\uff5c>\nOkay, let me tackle multiplying 391 by 251. I'll start with the standard multiplication method to get a clear step-by-step result.\n\nFirst, set up the multiplication vertically:\n\n```\n   391\n\u00d7 251\n-------\n```\n\nStarting with the units",
