 500 is 96,500. Subtract that from 100,939: 100,939 - 96,500 = 4,439.\n\nNow 193 * 20 is 3,860. Subtract that from 4,439: 4,439 - 3,860 = 579.\n\nThen 193 * 3 is 579. So total is 500 + 20 + 3 = 523. So that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, divide 100,939 by 523 to see if we get 193.\n\nLet me try that. 523 * 190 = ?\n\n523*200=104,600; subtract 523*10=5,230: so 104,600 -5,230 = 99,370.\n\nThen 523 * 3 = 1,569. So 193 is 190 +3. So 99,370 +1,569 = 100,939. Perfect.\n\nTherefore, all methods confirm that the product is 100,939.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 193 and 523 is \\boxed{100939}.\n\uff5c\n\nTo find the product of 193 and 523, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy. Here are the key steps:\n\n### 1. **Using the Distributive Property:**\n   - Break down 523 into 500 + 20 + 3.\n   - Calculate each part separately:\n     - \\(193 \\times 500 = 96,500\\)\n     - \\(193 \\times 20 = 3,860\\)\n     - \\(193 \\times 3 = 579\\)\n   - Sum the results:\n     - \\(96,500 + 3,860 = 100,360\\)\n     - \\(100,360 + 579 = 100,939\\)\n\n### 2. **Using the Standard Algorithm:**\n   - Multiply 193 by each digit of 523 (starting from the ones place):\n     - \\(193 \\times 3 = 579\\)\n     - \\(193 \\times 20 = 3,860\\) (shifted one position to the left)\n     - \\(193 \\times 500 = 96,500\\) (shifted two positions to the left)\n   - Sum the results:\n     - \\(579 + 3,860 = 4,439\\)\n     - \\(4,439 + 96,500 = 100,939\\)\n\n### 3. **Verification Using the Difference of Squares Method:**\n   - Express 193 as \\(200 - 7\\):\n     - \\(200 \\times 523 = 104,600\\)\n     - \\(7 \\times 523 = 3,661\\)\n   - Subtract the second result from the first:\n     - \\(104,600 - 3,661 = 100,939\\)\n\n### 4. **Verification by Division:**\n   - Divide the result by one of the factors:\n     - \\(100,939 \\div 193 = 523\\)\n     - \\(100,939 \\div 523 = 193\\)\n\nAll methods confirm that the product of 193 and 523 is \\(\\boxed{100939}\\).\uff5c\n\nThe product of 193 and 523 is \\box