messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 955 and 366?', '.\n\nThe product of 955 and 366 is calculated as follows:.\n\n1. **Break down the numbers using the distributive property:**.\n   - \\(955 \\times 366 = (900 + 50 + 5) \\times (300 + 60 + 6)\\).\n   .\n2. **Multiply each part and sum the results:**.\n   - \\(900 \\times 300 = 270,000\\).\n   - \\(900 \\times 60 = 54,000\\).\n   - \\(900 \\times 6 = 5,400\\).\n   - \\(50 \\times 300 = 15,000\\).\n   - \\(50 \\times 60 = 3,000\\).\n   - \\(50 \\times 6 = 300\\).\n   - \\(5 \\times 300 = 1,500\\).\n   - \\(5 \\times 60 = 300\\).\n   - \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\).\n\n3. **Sum all the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{align*}.\n   270,000 + 54,000 + 5,400 + 15,000 + 3,000 + 300 + 1,500 + 300 + 30 \\\\.\n   = 270,000 + 54,000 &= 324,000 \\\\.\n   324,000 + 5,400 &= 329,400 \\\\.\n   329,400 + 15,000 &= 344,400 \\\\.\n   344,400 + 3,000 &= 347,400 \\\\.\n   347,400 + 300 &= 347,700 \\\\.\n   347,700 + 1,500 &= 349,200 \\\\.\n   349,200 + 300 &= 349,500 \\\\.\n   349,500 + 30 &= 349,530.\n   \\end{align*}.\n   \\].\n\n4. **Verification using the standard algorithm:**.\n   - \\(955 \\times 6 = 5,730\\).\n   - \\(955 \\times 60 = 57,300\\).\n   - \\(955 \\times 300 = 286,500\\).\n   - Summing these: \\(5,730 + 57,300 + 286,500 = 349,530\\).\n\n**Final Answer:**. Therefore, the answer is ']]
