\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 955 and 366 is \\boxed{349530}.<\uff5c\n<\uff5c\n\nThe product of 955 and 366 is calculated by breaking down each number into its place values and using the distributive property. Here's the step-by-step solution:\n\n1. **Decompose the numbers:**\n   - \\(955 = 900 + 50 + 5\\)\n   - \\(366 = 300 + 60 + 6\\)\n\n2. **Multiply each part of the decomposed numbers:**\n   - \\(900 \\times 300 = 270,000\\)\n   - \\(900 \\times 60 = 54,000\\)\n   - \\(900 \\times 6 = 5,400\\)\n   - \\(50 \\times 300 = 15,000\\)\n   - \\(50 \\times 60 = 3,000\\)\n   - \\(50 \\times 6 = 300\\)\n   - \\(5 \\times 300 = 1,500\\)\n   - \\(5 \\times 60 = 300\\)\n   - \\(5 \\times 6 = 30\\)\n\n3. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   \\begin{align*}\n   270,000 + 54,000 + 5,400 + 15,000 + 3,000 + 300 + 1,500 + 300 + 30 \\\\\n   = 270,000 + 54,000 &= 324,000 \\\\\n   324,000 + 5,400 &= 329,400 \\\\\n   329,400 + 15,000 &= 344,400 \\\\\n   344,400 + 3,000 &= 347,400 \\\\\n   347,400 + 300 &= 347,700 \\\\\n   347,700 + 1,500 &= 349,200 \\\\\n   349,200 + 300 &= 349,500 \\\\\n   349,500 + 30 &= 349,530\n   \\end{align*}\n   \\]\n\n4. **Verification using the standard multiplication algorithm:**\n   - \\(955 \\times 6 = 5,730\\)\n   - \\(955 \\times 60 = 57,300\\)\n   - \\(955 \\times 300 = 286,500\\)\n   - Summing these results: \\(5,730 + 57,300 + 286,500 = 349,530\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm the product is **349,530**.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 955 and 366 is \\boxed{349530}.<\uff5c\n<\uff5c\n\nThe product of 955 and 366 is calculated by breaking down each number into its place values and using the distributive property. Here's the step-by-step solution:\n\n1. **Decompose the numbers:**\n   - \\(955 = 900 + 50 + 5\\)\n   - \\(366 = 300 + 60 + 6\\)\n\n2. **Multiply each part of the decomposed numbers:**\n   - \\(900 \\times 300 = 270,000\\)\n   - \\(900 \\times 60 = 54,000\\)\n   - \\(900 \\times 6 = 5,400\\)\n   - \\(50 \\times 300 = 15,000\\)\n   