messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 280 and 259?', '.\n\nTo find the product of 280 and 259, we can use multiple methods to ensure accuracy. Here are the key steps:.\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm:**.\n   - Multiply 280 by 9 (units place of 259):.\n     \\[.\n     280 \\times 9 = 2520.\n     \\].\n   - Multiply 280 by 50 (tens place of 259):.\n     \\[.\n     280 \\times 50 = 14000.\n     \\].\n   - Multiply 280 by 200 (hundreds place of 259):.\n     \\[.\n     280 \\times 200 = 56000.\n     \\].\n   - Sum the partial products:.\n     \\[.\n     2520 + 14000 + 56000 = 72520.\n     \\].\n\n2. **Breaking Down Numbers:**.\n   - Express 259 as \\(260 - 1\\):.\n     \\[.\n     280 \\times (260 - 1) = 280 \\times 260 - 280 \\times 1.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate \\(280 \\times 260\\):.\n     \\[.\n     280 \\times 200 = 56000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 280 \\times 60 = 16800.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     56000 + 16800 = 72800.\n     \\].\n   - Subtract 280:.\n     \\[.\n     72800 - 280 = 72520.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Distributive Property:**.\n   - Break down 280 into 200 and 80:.\n     \\[.\n     (200 + 80) \\times 259 = 200 \\times 259 + 80 \\times 259.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate each part:.\n     \\[.\n     200 \\times 259 = 51800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 80 \\times 259 = 20720.\n     \\].\n   - Sum the results:.\n     \\[.\n     51800 + 20720 = 72520.\n     \\]. Therefore, the answer is ']]
