      "text": "508,378. Wait, let me check that again. Hmm, maybe I made a mistake in adding. Let me recalculate:\n\nFirst, let me verify each multiplication step again to ensure there are no errors.\n\nStarting with 821 \u00d7 600:\n\n800 \u00d7 600 is indeed 480,000.\n\n20 \u00d7 600 is 12,000.\n\n1 \u00d7 600 is 600. Adding those together: 480,000 + 12,000 = 492,000; then +600 gives 492,600. That's correct.\n\nNext, 821 \u00d7 10 is straightforward: 8,210. Correct.\n\nThen, 821 \u00d7 8:\n\n800 \u00d78 = 6,400.\n\n20 \u00d78 = 160.\n\n1\u00d78 =8. Adding those: 6,400 +160 = 6,560 +8 =6,568. That's correct.\n\nNow, adding all three components:\n\nFirst, 492,600 + 8,210. Let's add 492,600 + 8,000 first, which is 500,600, then add the remaining 210: 500,600 +210 = 500,810. Then add 6,568 to that.\n\n500,810 +6,568:\n\nAdding 500,810 +6,000 =506,810.\n\nThen add 568: 506,810 +568 =507,378.\n\nWait, that's different from my initial thought of 508,378. Hmm, so my first addition had an error. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 500,810 + 6,568:\n\nBreakdown:\n\n500,810 +6,000 =506,810.\n\nThen 506,810 +568 = 506,810 + 500 =507,310, then +68 =507,378.\n\nYes, so the correct total is 507,378.\n\nTherefore, the final product of 821 and 618 is 507,378.\n\nBut wait, let me confirm using another method to ensure accuracy.\n\nAlternative approach: Multiply 821 \u00d7618 directly using the standard algorithm.\n\nFirst, write down 821\n\n\u00d7618\n\n________\n\nMultiply 821 by 8: 6,568.\n\nMultiply 821 by 1 (tens place): 821 \u00d710 =8,210.\n\nMultiply 821 by 6 (hundreds place): 821 \u00d7600=492,600.\n\nNow add them together:\n\n6,568\n\n8,210\n\n492,600\n\nAdding the first two: 6,568 +8,210 =14,778.\n\nThen add to 492,600: 492,600 +14,778 =507,378. Yes, same result.\n\nAlternatively, using another verification method: (800 +21)(600 +18).\n\nExpand this as:\n\n800\u00d7600 +800\u00d718 +21\u00d7600 +21\u00d718.\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n800\u00d7600 =480,000.\n\n800\u00d718 =14,400.\n\n21\u00d7600=12,600.\n\n21\u00d718=378.\n\nAdding all these together:\n\n480,000 +14,400 =494,400.\n\n494,400 +12,600 =507,000.\n\n507,000 +378 =507,378. Same result.\n\nTherefore, the correct product is 507,378.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 821 and 618 is \\boxed{507378}.\n<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>\n\nTo find the product of 821 and 618, we use the distributive property by breaking down each number into hundreds, tens, and ones:\n\n\\[\n821 = 800 + 20 + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n618 = 600 + 10 + 8\n\\]\n\nWe then multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number and sum the results:\n\n1. Calculate \\(821 \\times 600\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 600 = (800 + 20 + 1) \\times 600 = 800 \\times 600 + 20 \\times 600 + 1 \\times 600 = 480000 + 12000 + 600 = 492600\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(821 \\times 10\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 10 = 8210\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(821 \\times 8\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 8 = (800 + 20 + 1) \\times 8 = 800 \\times 8 + 20 \\times 8 + 1 \\times 8 = 6400 + 160 + 8 = 6568\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these products:\n\n\\[\n492600 + 8210 + 6568\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n\n1. Add \\(492600 + 8210\\):\n   \\[\n   492600 + 8210 = 500810\n   \\]\n\n2. Add the result to \\(6568\\):\n   \\[\n   500810 + 6568 = 507378\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the standard algorithm confirms the result:\n- Multiply 821 by 8: \\(6568\\)\n- Multiply 821 by 10: \\(8210\\)\n- Multiply 821 by 600: \\(492600\\)\n- Sum these results: \\(6568 + 8210 + 492600 = 507378\\)\n\nAnother verification using the expansion \\((800 + 21)(600 + 18)\\) also confirms the result:\n- \\(800 \\times 600 = 480000\\)\n- \\(800 \\times 18 = 14400\\)\n- \\(21 \\times 600 = 12600\\)\n- \\(21 \\times 18 = 378\\)\n- Sum these results: \\(480000 + 14400 + 12600 + 378 = 507378\\)\n\nThus, the product of 821 and 618 is \\(\\boxed{507378}\\).<\uff5cAssistant\uff5c> The product of 821 and 618 is \\boxed{507378}.<\uff5c\n\nTo find the product