 492600\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(821 \\times 10\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 10 = 8210\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(821 \\times 8\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 8 = (800 + 20 + 1) \\times 8 = 800 \\times 8 + 20 \\times 8 + 1 \\times 8 = 6400 + 160 + 8 = 6568\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these products:\n\n\\[\n492600 + 8210 + 6568\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n\n1. Add \\(492600 + 8210\\):\n   \\[\n   492600 + 8210 = 500810\n   \\]\n\n2. Add the result to \\(6568\\):\n   \\[\n   500810 + 6568 = 507378\n   \\]\n\nVerification using the standard algorithm confirms the result:\n- Multiply 821 by 8: \\(6568\\)\n- Multiply 821 by 10: \\(8210\\)\n- Multiply 821 by 600: \\(492600\\)\n- Sum these results: \\(6568 + 8210 + 492600 = 507378\\)\n\nAnother verification using the expansion \\((800 + 21)(600 + 18)\\) also confirms the result:\n- \\(800 \\times 600 = 480000\\)\n- \\(800 \\times 18 = 14400\\)\n- \\(21 \\times 600 = 12600\\)\n- \\(21 \\times 18 = 378\\)\n- Sum these results: \\(480000 + 14400 + 12600 + 378 = 507378\\)\n\nThus, the product of 821 and 618 is \\boxed{507378}.<\uff5c\n\nTo find the product of 821 and 618, we use the distributive property by breaking down each number into hundreds, tens, and ones:\n\n\\[\n821 = 800 + 20 + 1\n\\]\n\\[\n618 = 600 + 10 + 8\n\\]\n\nWe then multiply each part of the first number by each part of the second number and sum the results:\n\n1. Calculate \\(821 \\times 600\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 600 = (800 + 20 + 1) \\times 600 = 800 \\times 600 + 20 \\times 600 + 1 \\times 600 = 480000 + 12000 + 600 = 492600\n   \\]\n\n2. Calculate \\(821 \\times 10\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 10 = 8210\n   \\]\n\n3. Calculate \\(821 \\times 8\\):\n   \\[\n   821 \\times 8 = (800 + 20 + 1) \\times 8 = 800 \\times 8 + 20 \\times 8 + 1 \\times 8 = 6400 + 160 + 8 = 6568\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these products:\n\n\\[\n492600 + 8210 + 6568\n\\]\n\nBreaking down the addition step-by-step:\n\n1. Add \\(492600 