ple-checking gives me confidence.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 338,826.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 758 and 447 is \\boxed{338826}.\n<\uff5cend\uff5estream\uff5eoutput\uff5c>\n\nTo find the product of 758 and 447, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply by the units place (7):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 7 = 5306\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (40):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 40 = 30320\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (400):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 400 = 303200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   5306 + 30320 + 303200 = 338826\n   \\]\n\nThe product is verified through multiple methods, confirming the result is consistent.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{338826}\n\\]\uff5c>\n<\uff5c\n\nThe product of 758 and 447 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into manageable parts and summing the results:\n\n1. **Multiply by the units place:**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 7 = 5306\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (shifted one position left):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 40 = 30320\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (shifted two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 400 = 303200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   5306 + 30320 + 303200 = 338826\n   \\]\n\nThe final result is verified through multiple methods, confirming the answer is consistent.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{338826}\n\\]\uff5c>\n<\uff5c\n\nThe product of 758 and 447 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into manageable parts and summing the results:\n\n1. **Multiply by the units place:**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 7 = 5306\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply by the tens place (shifted one position left):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 40 = 30320\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply by the hundreds place (shifted two positions left):**\n   \\[\n   758 \\times 400 = 303200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   5306 + 30320 + 303200 = 338826\n   \\]\n\nThe final result is verified through multiple methods, conf