      "text": "294,984.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 612 and 482 is \\boxed{294984}.\n<\uff5c>/\n\nTo find the product of 612 and 482, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\n**Standard Algorithm:**\n1. Multiply 612 by 2 (units place):\n   \\[\n   612 \\times 2 = 1224\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 612 by 80 (tens place):\n   \\[\n   612 \\times 8 = 4896 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 48960\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 612 by 400 (hundreds place):\n   \\[\n   612 \\times 4 = 2448 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 244800\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   1224 + 48960 + 244800\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(1224 + 48960\\):\n     \\[\n     1224 + 48960 = 50184\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(244800\\):\n     \\[\n     50184 + 244800 = 294984\n     \\]\n\n**Verification using the distributive property:**\n\\[\n(600 + 12)(500 - 18) = 600 \\times 500 + 600 \\times (-18) + 12 \\times 500 + 12 \\times (-18)\n\\]\n\\[\n= 300000 - 10800 + 6000 - 216\n\\]\n\\[\n= 300000 - 10800 = 289200\n\\]\n\\[\n289200 + 6000 = 295200\n\\]\n\\[\n295200 - 216 = 294984\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result. Therefore, the product of 612 and 482 is \\boxed{294984}. <\uff5c\n\nTo find the product of 612 and 482, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify using the distributive property.\n\n**Standard Algorithm:**\n1. Multiply 612 by 2 (units place):\n   \\[\n   612 \\times 2 = 1224\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 612 by 80 (tens place):\n   \\[\n   612 \\times 8 = 4896 \\quad \\text{(then add a zero)} \\quad 48960\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 612 by 400 (hundreds place):\n   \\[\n   612 \\times 4 = 2448 \\quad \\text{(then add two zeros)} \\quad 244800\n   \\]\n\n4. Add the results of the three multiplications:\n   \\[\n   1224 + 48960 + 244800\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(1224 + 48960\\):\n     \\[\n     1224 + 48960 = 50184\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(244800\\):\n  