messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 596 and 273?', '.\n\nTo find the product of 596 and 273, we use the standard multiplication algorithm:.\n\n1. **Multiply 596 by 3 (ones place):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     596 \\\\.\n   \\times \\ 3 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     1788 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - 3 × 6 = 18 (write 8, carry over 1).\n   - 3 × 9 = 27 + 1 = 28 (write 8, carry over 2).\n   - 3 × 5 = 15 + 2 = 17 (write 17).\n\n2. **Multiply 596 by 70 (tens place):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     596 \\\\.\n   \\times 70 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     41720 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - 7 × 6 = 42 (write 2, carry over 4).\n   - 7 × 9 = 63 + 4 = 67 (write 7, carry over 6).\n   - 7 × 5 = 35 + 6 = 41 (write 41).\n   - Shift one position to the left (multiply by 10).\n\n3. **Multiply 596 by 200 (hundreds place):**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     596 \\\\.\n   \\times 200 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     119200 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - 2 × 6 = 12 (write 2, carry over 1).\n   - 2 × 9 = 18 + 1 = 19 (write 9, carry over 1).\n   - 2 × 5 = 10 + 1 = 11 (write 11).\n   - Shift two positions to the left (multiply by 100).\n\n4. **Add the partial products:**.\n   \\[.\n   \\begin{array}{r}.\n     1788 \\\\.\n   + 41720 \\\\.\n   + 119200 \\\\.\n   \\hline.\n     162708 \\\\.\n   \\end{array}.\n   \\].\n   - Adding the units place: 8 + 0 + 0 = 8.\n   - Tens place: 8 + 2 + 0 = 10 (write 0, carry over 1).\n   - Hundreds place: 7 + 7 + 2 + 1 = 17 (write 7, carry over 1).\n   - Thousands place: 1 + 1 + 9 + 1 = 12 (write 2, carry over 1).\n   - Ten thousands place: 0 + 4 + 1 + 1 = 6.\n   - Hundred thousands place: 1. Therefore, the answer is ']]
