 carry over 1.  \n- **Tens place:**  \n  \\( 2 \\times 9 = 18 \\). Add the carried-over 1: \\( 18 + 1 = 19 \\). Write down 9, carry over 1.  \n- **Hundreds place:**  \n  \\( 2 \\times 5 = 10 \\). Add the carried-over 1: \\( 10 + 1 = 11 \\). Write down 11.  \n\nThis gives \\( 596 \\times 2 = 1192 \\). Shifting two places left: **119,200**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Add All Partial Products\nNow, add the three results together:\n\n```\n     1788\n   +41720\n   +119200\n   ---------\n```\n\n**Adding the first two numbers:**  \n\\( 1788 + 41,720 = 43,508 \\).\n\n**Adding the third number:**  \n\\( 43,508 + 119,200 = 162,708 \\).\n\n---\n\n### Verification\nTo ensure accuracy, I'll verify using another method. Breaking down 273 into \\( 200 + 70 + 3 \\):\n\n\\[\n596 \\times 273 = 596 \\times (200 + 70 + 3) = 596 \\times 200 + 596 \\times 70 + 596 \\times 3\n\\]\n\nCalculating each term:\n- \\( 596 \\times 200 = 119,200 \\)\n- \\( 596 \\times 70 = 41,720 \\)\n- \\( 596 \\times 3 = 1,788 \\)\n\nAdding them together:\n\\[\n119,200 + 41,720 = 160,920 \\\\\n160,920 + 1,788 = 162,708\n\\]\n\nBoth methods give the same result. \n\n---\n\n**Final Answer**  \nThe product of 596 and 273 is \\boxed{162708}.\n<\uff5c/User\uff5c>\n\nOkay, so I need to multiply 596 by 273. Let me start by writing the numbers vertically:\n\n```\n   596\n\u00d7 273\n-------\n```\n\n### Step 1: Multiply by the Ones Place (3)\nFirst, multiply 596 by the digit in the ones place of 273, which is 3.\n\n- **Units place:**  \n  \\( 3 \\times 6 = 18 \\). Write down 8, carry over 1.  \n- **Tens place:**  \n  \\( 3 \\times 9 = 27 \\). Add the carried-over 1: \\( 27 + 1 = 28 \\). Write down 8, carry over 2.  \n- **Hundreds place:**  \n  \\( 3 \\times 5 = 15 \\). Add the carried-over 2: \\( 15 + 2 = 17 \\). Write down 17.  \n\nResult: \\( 596 \\times 3 = 1788 \\).\n\n---\n\n### Step 2: Multiply by the Tens Place (70)\nNext, multiply 596 by the digit in the tens place (7, representing 70). Shift the result one place left.\n\n- **Units place:**  \n  \\( 7 \\times 6 = 42 \\). Write down 2, carry over 4.  \n- **Tens place:**  \n  \\( 7 \\times 9 = 63 \\). Add carried-over 4: \\( 63 + 4 = 67 \\). Write down 7, carry over 6.  \n- **Hundreds place:**  \n  \\( 7 \\times 5 = 35 \\). Add carried-over 6: \\( 35 + 6 = 41 \\). Write down 41.  \n\nResult: \\( 596 \\times 7 = 4172 \\). Shifted: **41,720**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Multiply by the Hundreds Place (200)\nMultiply 596 by the hundreds digit (2, representing 200). Shift two places left.\n\n- **Units place:**  \n  \\( 2 \\times 6 = 12 \\). Write down 2, carry over 1.  \n- **Tens place:**  \n  \\( 2 \\times 9 = 18 \\). Add carried-over 1: \\( 19 \\). Write down 9, carry over 1.  \n- **Hundreds place:**  \n  \\( 2 \\times 5 = 10 \\). Add carried-over 1: \\( 11 \\). Write down 11.  \n\nResult: \\( 596 \\times 2 = 1192 \\). Shifted: **119,200**.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: Add Partial Products\n```\n     1788\n   +41720\n   +119200\n   ---------\n```\n\n- **First addition:**  \n  \\( 1788 + 41,720 = 43,508 \\).  \n- **Second addition:**  \n  \\( 43,508 + 119,200 = 162,708 \\).\n\n---\n\n### Verification\nUsing distributive property:  \n\\[\n596 \\times 273 = 596 \\times (200 + 70 + 3) = 119,200 + 41,720 + 1,788 = 162,708\n\\]\n\nBoth methods confirm the result.\n\n**Final Answer**  \nThe product of 596 and 273 is \\boxed{162708}.\n<\uff5c/User\uff5c> <\uff5cAssistant\uff5c>Okay, so I need to multiply 596 by 273. Let me start by writing the numbers vertically:\n\n```\n   596\n\u00d7 273\n-------\n```\n\n### Step 1: Multiply by the Ones Place (3)\nFirst, multiply 596 by the digit in the ones place of 273, which is 3.\n\n- **Units place:**  \n  \\( 3 \\times 6 = 18 \\). Write down 8, carry over 1.  \n- **Tens place:**  \n  \\( 3 \\times 9 = 27 \\). Add the carried-over 1: \\( 27 + 1 = 28 \\). Write down 8, carry over 2.  \n- **Hundreds place:**  \n  \\( 3 \\times 5 = 15 \\). Add the carried-over 2: \\( 15 + 2 = 17 \\). Write down 17.  \n\nResult: \\(