messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 124 and 912?', '.\n\nTo find the product of 124 and 912, we can use the distributive property and the standard algorithm for multiplication. Here are the key steps:.\n\n1. **Using the distributive property:**.\n   - Break down 912 into 900 and 12.\n   - Calculate \\(124 \\times 900\\):.\n     \\[.\n     124 \\times 9 = 1116 \\quad \\text{then} \\quad 1116 \\times 100 = 111600.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate \\(124 \\times 12\\):.\n     \\[.\n     124 \\times 10 = 1240 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 124 \\times 2 = 248.\n     \\].\n     \\[.\n     1240 + 248 = 1488.\n     \\].\n   - Add the results:.\n     \\[.\n     111600 + 1488 = 113088.\n     \\].\n\n2. **Using the standard algorithm:**.\n   - Multiply 124 by each digit of 912 (starting from the right):.\n     - \\(124 \\times 2 = 248\\).\n     - \\(124 \\times 10 = 1240\\).\n     - \\(124 \\times 900 = 111600\\).\n   - Sum the results with appropriate shifts:.\n     \\[.\n     248 + 1240 + 111600 = 113088.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Verification using another method (expanding both numbers):**.\n   - Break down both numbers into their place values and multiply each term:.\n     \\[.\n     (100 + 20 + 4) \\times (900 + 10 + 2).\n     \\]. Therefore, the answer is ']]
