messages:  [['Please solve the math problem.\nQuestion: What is the Product of 294 and 410?', '.\n\nTo find the product of 294 and 410, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm and verify it with different methods:.\n\n1. **Standard Multiplication Algorithm**:.\n   - Multiply 294 by 0 (units place): \\(294 \\times 0 = 0\\).\n   - Multiply 294 by 1 (tens place) and shift one position left: \\(294 \\times 1 = 294 \\rightarrow 2940\\).\n   - Multiply 294 by 4 (hundreds place) and shift two positions left: \\(294 \\times 4 = 1176 \\rightarrow 117600\\).\n   - Add the partial products: \\(0 + 2940 + 117600 = 120540\\).\n\n2. **Distributive Property**:.\n   - Break down 410 into 400 and 10:.\n     \\[.\n     294 \\times 410 = 294 \\times (400 + 10) = (294 \\times 400) + (294 \\times 10).\n     \\].\n   - Calculate each term:.\n     \\[.\n     294 \\times 400 = 117600 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 294 \\times 10 = 2940.\n     \\].\n   - Sum the results:.\n     \\[.\n     117600 + 2940 = 120540.\n     \\].\n\n3. **Verification by Prime Factorization**:.\n   - Factorize both numbers:.\n     \\[.\n     294 = 2 \\times 3 \\times 7^2 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 410 = 2 \\times 5 \\times 41.\n     \\].\n   - Multiply the factors:.\n     \\[.\n     (2 \\times 3 \\times 7^2) \\times (2 \\times 5 \\times 41) = 2^2 \\times 3 \\times 5 \\times 7^2 \\times 41.\n     \\].\n   - Calculate step-by-step:.\n     \\[.\n     2^2 = 4, \\quad 4 \\times 3 = 12, \\quad 12 \\times 5 = 60, \\quad 60 \\times 49 = 2940, \\quad 2940 \\times 41 = 120540.\n     \\].\n\n4. **Cross-Verification by Division**:.\n   - Divide the result by one of the numbers to check if it gives the other:.\n     \\[.\n     120540 \\div 294 = 410.\n     \\]. Therefore, the answer is ']]
